      "writtenOn": "2025-10-23T14:51:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Somewhat orthogonal question: I wonder if avoiding introducing a new callback type is also an option.  I guess that we can\u0027t easily reuse `SkSerialImageProc` because serializing `SkImage` (i.e. getting the `SkPixmap`) may require `Gr...Context` which is not handled by the callback today.\n\nBut maybe we should still introduce a new callback type in a XPS/SVG-agnostic way - e.g. introducing `SkSerialPixmapProc`.",
      "revId": "9529ec2c0dd174527fa9ded88f4ca6bde0219e87",
